      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg a day is twice the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg a day. A 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the normal range. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. A prescriber with authority over this patient needs to confirm an order like this.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Ask the prescriber to enter or confirm the order directly. If they intend a dose this far above the usual maximum, they should document the clinical rationale. Pharmacy would also normally review it.\n- If the intended dose was 850 mg three times daily, or 1,700 mg a day in total, tell me. A prescriber still needs to be the source of the order.\n\nI'm glad to help once there's a clinician-confirmed, safe order."
      }
